   - Use the Npcap API to capture packets and decode them. Here’s an example of how you might start writing this code:

```csharp
using System;
using System.ServiceProcess;
using Npcap;

public class NetworkTrafficDecoder : ServiceBase
{
    private NpcapDevice _device;

    public NetworkTrafficDecoder()
    {
        // Initialize the device
        _device = NpcapDevice.OpenDefault();
    }

    protected override void OnStart(string[] args)
    {
        // Start capturing packets
        _device.StartCapture();

        // Your decoding logic goes here
        while (true)
        {
            var packet = _device.ReadPacket();
            if (packet != null)
            {
                // Decode the packet and process it
                ProcessPacket(packet);
            }
        }
    }

    protected override void OnStop()
    {
        // Stop capturing packets
        _device.StopCapture();
    }

    private void ProcessPacket(Packet packet)
    {
        // Implement your packet processing logic here
        Console.WriteLine($"Packet captured: {packet}");
    }
}
```

5. **Configure the Service**:
   - In the `OnStart` method, configure the service to start capturing packets.
   - In the `OnStop` method, ensure that the service stops capturing packets when it is stopped.

6. **Build and Deploy the Service**:
   - Build your project to generate the executable file.
   - Copy the generated executable to the appropriate directory where Windows services are managed (usually `C:\Windows\System32\Services.msc`).

7. **Install the Service**:
